12. BACKTEST LAB
==================================================

Implement a genuine backtesting engine, not a chart populated with arbitrary performance numbers.

Requirements:
- Walk-forward evaluation.
- Chronological train/test separation.
- Frozen strategy configurations.
- Sealed holdout evaluation.
- Signal at time t and execution no earlier than the configured executable time, such as t+1.
- Realistic transaction costs.
- Slippage assumptions.
- Contract rollover handling.
- Liquidity constraints.
- Position sizing.
- Margin and exposure checks.
- Missing-data handling.
- Trade logs.
- Equity curve.
- Drawdown curve.
- Gross versus net P&L.
- Sharpe ratio with documented assumptions.
- Hit rate.
- Turnover.
- Trade count.
- Average win and loss.
- Maximum drawdown.
- Confidence intervals.
- Block bootstrap or other appropriate uncertainty analysis.
- Minimum detectable effect (MDE), where methodologically appropriate.

Prevent future data from influencing historical decisions.

Freeze configurations before holdout evaluation and log configuration hashes.

Clearly label every metric according to whether it comes from real historical backtesting, an illustrative example, or a simulation.

Never fabricate performance, Sharpe ratios, win rates, or returns.

